# EV Motion — environment variables.
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is gitignored; this file is not.

# --- Site origin -------------------------------------------------------------
# The canonical origin, used for metadataBase, every canonical tag, the sitemap
# and JSON-LD urls. REQUIRED before going live.
#
# Leave it unset and the app falls back to the Vercel deployment URL, or (off
# Vercel) to a placeholder — and while the placeholder is in use, robots.txt
# disallows all crawling on purpose, because canonical tags pointing at a domain
# you don't own are worse for indexing than not being crawled. See src/lib/site.ts.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.com

# --- Supabase (lead capture) -------------------------------------------------
# Storage for enquiries submitted through the site's lead-capture CTAs.
#
# Until BOTH of these are set, POST /api/leads validates and rate-limits the
# submission but stores nothing, and every lead dialog says so instead of
# showing a confirmation it can't back up. Nothing breaks while they're unset.
#
# The same credentials also back first-party analytics (POST /api/events) —
# there is no separate key for it. Run BOTH migrations in supabase/migrations/
# (0001_leads.sql and 0003_analytics_events.sql) before setting these; 0002 is
# only for publishable-key setups, see its header.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co

# Then pick ONE of the two keys below.
#
# PREFERRED — the secret key (`sb_secret_…`, or a legacy service_role JWT).
# Bypasses RLS, so 0001_leads.sql's deny-all policy set stands and /api/leads
# is the ONLY path that can write a lead. SERVER-SIDE ONLY: never prefix it
# with NEXT_PUBLIC_, never commit it, never reference it from a "use client"
# file. Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API keys -> Secret keys.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=sb_secret_...

# ALTERNATIVE — the publishable key (`sb_publishable_…`, or a legacy anon
# JWT). Public by design and subject to RLS, so it ALSO requires running
# supabase/migrations/0002_leads_publishable_key_policy.sql. Understand the
# trade-off first: anyone holding this key can POST rows straight to
# PostgREST, skipping this app's validation, honeypot and rate limiting.
# Ignored when a secret key is also set.
# SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_...

# --- ImageKit ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Vehicle photo delivery. Infrastructure is wired up (see VehicleImage.tsx) but
# no vehicle has photo data yet, so the app renders branded placeholders and
# runs fine with these unset.
#
# The URL endpoint's account id must also be allow-listed in next.config.ts's
# images.remotePatterns — update it there if the account ever changes.
NEXT_PUBLIC_IMAGEKIT_URL_ENDPOINT=https://ik.imagekit.io/your_account_id
NEXT_PUBLIC_IMAGEKIT_PUBLIC_KEY=public_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Server-side only — never prefix this one with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
IMAGEKIT_PRIVATE_KEY=private_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# --- Error monitoring (Sentry) -----------------------------------------------
# Entirely optional. With no DSN the app behaves exactly as it did before
# Sentry was installed: the SDK is never initialised, its chunk is never
# fetched by the browser (verified — 319 KB of JS without, 503 KB with), and
# next.config.ts skips the build plugin altogether.
#
# Server errors are recorded into `analytics_events` either way, via
# src/instrumentation.ts's onRequestError -> lib/monitoring/serverErrors.ts.
# Sentry adds what that pipeline was never meant to be: something that can
# alert a human (CLAUDE.md #25).
#
# To enable: create a project at sentry.io (Next.js platform), copy its DSN.
# A DSN is a write-only ingest endpoint, not a secret — NEXT_PUBLIC_ is correct.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SENTRY_DSN=https://<key>@<org>.ingest.<region>.sentry.io/<project>

# Optional, and only used to upload source maps at build time so stack traces
# are readable instead of minified. Set these in the Vercel environment —
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN is a real secret and must never be committed. Without the
# token, error capture still works; you just get minified traces.
# SENTRY_ORG=your-org-slug
# SENTRY_PROJECT=your-project-slug
# SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=sntrys_...

# --- Lead notifications -------------------------------------------------------
# Optional. Without it, a submitted enquiry sits in `public.leads` until someone
# opens the Supabase dashboard — which, since that table is RLS deny-all with no
# admin UI, means enquiries can go unnoticed for days.
#
# Any incoming-webhook URL works: Slack, Discord, Google Chat, Microsoft Teams,
# Zapier, Make, n8n. The payload sends both `text` and `content` so one variable
# fits all of them.
#
# ⚠️ This sends the submitter's NAME and CONTACT DETAILS to whatever URL you set.
# That is deliberate — a notification you have to go and look something up from
# does not solve the problem — but the destination must be a private channel
# your team controls. See /privacy, which discloses this as a service provider.
#
# A failing or slow webhook can never cost you the lead: storage happens first,
# the notifier never throws, and it gives up after 2.5s.
# LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL=https://hooks.slack.com/services/T000/B000/xxxxxxxx

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Pricing service configuration  (all OPTIONAL)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Every rate, tenure and tariff the site quotes is resolved by
# src/lib/vehicle-pricing/config.ts. Unset variables fall back to the
# documented defaults there — a stock deployment needs none of these.
#
# Set one to change a figure site-wide (Vehicle Detail Page, Compare, listing
# cards, homepage) without touching code. A malformed or out-of-range value is
# ignored with a dev-time warning and the default is used, so a typo can never
# turn a price into NaN.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is required: the VDP's EMI calculator runs in the browser.
# These are public rates printed on the page — never put a secret here.

# Finance — the assumption behind every "EMI from ₹X/mo" figure.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICING_ANNUAL_RATE_PCT=9.5        # annual reducing-balance rate, %
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICING_TENURE_MONTHS=60           # tenure behind the headline EMI
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICING_DOWN_PAYMENT_PCT=20        # down payment behind it, %

# Finance — bounds of the VDP sidebar's EMI sliders.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICING_TENURE_MIN_MONTHS=36
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICING_TENURE_MAX_MONTHS=84
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICING_TENURE_STEP_MONTHS=12
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICING_DOWN_MIN_PCT=0
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICING_DOWN_MAX_PCT=40
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICING_DOWN_STEP_PCT=5

# Running cost — the tariffs the ownership calculators disclose on screen.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICING_ELECTRICITY_PER_UNIT=8     # ₹ per kWh
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICING_PETROL_PER_LITRE=105       # ₹ per litre
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PRICING_DAYS_PER_MONTH=30
#
# The per-category daily distance and petrol comparator (a car at 15 km/l, a
# scooter at 45, a commercial vehicle at 12) are structural rather than single
# numbers, so they live in PRICING_DEFAULTS rather than behind a variable.
